&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the rear of this house excavated in 1899 was a courtyard garden (a) with a &lt;em&gt;portico&lt;/em&gt; on the south. This was supported by one column that was reinforced by a large pillar. The garden was enclosed by a low wall with an opening on the south. A gutter that encircled the edges had a settling basin (0.35 x 0.45 m.; 0.55 m. deep) in the southwest corner. There was no cistern, but a &lt;em&gt;puteal&lt;/em&gt; stood in the southeast corner.&lt;/p&gt;
